#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Compare tools/server/'s data layer with upstream's server-common,
server-task and server-schema (Stage 10 step 3a).

`harness/server_task_ref.cpp` compiles beside upstream's `server-common.cpp`,
`server-task.cpp`, `server-schema.cpp` and `server-chat.cpp`, unmodified,
over the libraries `zig build tools-ref` installs; `harness/server_task_diff.zig`
is the port's (`zig build server-task-diff-bins`). Both read the same records
and write one transcript each, which must be identical, and log through
`common_log` at debug verbosity with a marker per record, so stderr must be
identical too.

The records, generated here from a fixed seed:
- B   params_base members (n_parallel, antiprompt, verbosity, samplers, ...)
- P   a request through eval_llama_cmpl_schema, then task_params::to_json
      both ways and every member to_json leaves out -- upstream's own test
      payloads (tests/unit/*.py, read with `ast`, never run) and random and
      mutated ones over every field and alias
- O   oaicompat_completion_params_parse
- C   oaicompat_chat_params_parse on the legacy (--no-jinja) path: media
      parts as data URIs, bare base64 and file:// under a media path; and
      through Jinja over every template in models/templates/ (tools, tool
      choice, schemas, reasoning, kwargs, continuation, pure content)
- CS  a Jinja chat request into its chat session (dumped whole, and what
      it applies to a task's sampling), through the schema into a task
      with the session applied, and into a task_result_state; then R
      partials and a final fed a reply in pieces, as text or tokenized
      (common_chat_input_tokenize): the request's own PEG parser, streamed
      (Stage 10 step 4; v0.7.0's chat session)
- RC, AC, TC  server-chat.cpp's conversions: Responses, Anthropic and
      transcriptions requests into /chat/completions bodies
- T   tokenize_input_prompts / tokenize_mixed over six vocabularies, and
      with an mmproj; M  process_mtmd_prompt; ST  server_tokens ops
- U   validate_utf8 and is_valid_utf8 over every 1- and 2-byte string and
      3- and 4-byte strings over the bytes that matter
- S/R task_result_state (over the default session) and every result type
      in every response format,
      partials streamed through a state; the SSE formatters
- E, GT, F, K, I, Q, G, PC, PIPE, L, J, SSE, RND, TK -- error responses,
      grammar triggers, embeddings and rerank responses, infill and rerank
      prompts, token probabilities, the prompt cache, server_pipe, LoRA,
      nested json, random ids, tasks

Masked on both sides: `created`/`created_at`/`completed_at` (std::time),
the 32-character random ids after `resp_`, `rs_`, `msg_`, `chatcmpl-`, and
`%p` pointers in the prompt cache's trace log.

Usage: scripts/server-task-diff
  SERVER_TASK_N=<n>      records per random kind (default 300)
  SERVER_TASK_SEED=<n>   the generator's seed (default 1)
  SERVER_TASK_OUT=<dir>  keep the inputs, transcripts and logs there
  SERVER_TASK_NOBUILD=1  use the binaries already built in the out dir /
                         zig-out (for fault injection loops)
  SERVER_TASK_PORT_BIN   with it, this port binary: a build to a private prefix
"""

